<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ludwigstrasse</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ludwigstraße</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ludwigstrasse is a monumental avenue in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a>, laid out for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-i-of-bavaria">Ludwig I of Bavaria</a> from 1816, running north from the Odeonsplatz and the Feldherrnhalle to the Siegestor. Its southern part was designed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-von-klenze">Leo von Klenze</a> and its northern part by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-von-gartner">Friedrich von Gärtner</a>, who built the Bavarian State Library, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwigskirche">Ludwigskirche</a> and the university buildings along it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ludwigstrasse.jpg" alt="Ludwigstrasse" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gryffindor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludwigstra%C3%9Fe,_M%C3%BCnchen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
